WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.980
<b><i>We look the same, but men call us monsters. 

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.230
Oh, dear...

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.400
Who's there?!

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.970
Perhaps, now, your treason will be revealed.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.730
Damn you—

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.730
Hello again, Suruga-sama.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.190
Wh-Who are you?

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:34.010
Oh, my. Have you forgotten me?

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.020
Suruga-sama, it is I.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.260
J-Joujin...

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.920
E-Everyone, come here! Intruder!

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.000
I won't let you fool me again.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.290
I will never...

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.140
Suruga-sama,

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.930
first, put away your sword and sit.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:12.050
We might be talking for a while.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.640
I was a fool...

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.320
It was only a moment,

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.310
but your honeyed words deceived me.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:32.210
And I thought to take my 
brother's place as ruler.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:39.240
I never spoke to you of anything as simple

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.940
as becoming ruler of Japan.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:42.950
What?

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:50.960
I told you to become a god who rules.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.320
The forest... The forest moved!

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:02.470
You said that my wish would come 
true, unless the forest moved...

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.720
But it did!

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:08.150
Those were mere monkeys.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:14.730
Just groups of monkeys that were 
seeking a new place to live.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.770
You know this.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:22.410
You slew so many of them.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:29.920
The moving forest was simply 
a fantasy of yours.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.300
Tadanaga-sama, get a hold of yourself.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:40.890
Such weakness will only put you in danger.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:46.730
I cannot have a man who wanted 
to be a god feeling such things.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:52.030
A god commands, and all the 
laws of this world change.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:57.840
Suruga-sama, that is what you must be! A god!

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:02.700
But a man cannot become a god...

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.350
Was there not such a one?

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:10.630
A man who became as close 
to a god as one could be.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:15.240
Oda Kazusanosuke Nobunaga-sama!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:54.940
<b><i>The Butterfly Dances</i></b>

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.800
When I see you in my dreams,

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.060
it seems it is because

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:45.570
you are telling me to die for love.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:18.730
The hell you saw was no illusion.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.650
It is real.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.530
It is the true hell.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.660
<i>There are too many.</i>

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:03.420
Rui ran this way, right?

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:04.310
I think so.

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:34.320
Let's go.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.350
Yeah.

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:43.980
Well done, Utsutsu...

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:46.790
Do you think you can learn anything?

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.860
I'll have to take a closer look.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.790
This is fascinating, though.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:56.870
Those girls are crazy.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.790
They almost put themselves in danger.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:03.130
Then you came back at the perfect time.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:17.890
I thought we'd never bathe together again.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.140
Indeed, it's strange.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:23.650
They called themselves the Rain.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.440
Who are they?

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:26.460
The Rain?

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:30.150
A group of brigands who attacked us.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:33.880
Well, regardless,

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:37.190
you and Namenba saved us, this time.

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:39.000
You owe us.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.660
Yeah. I promise to repay you.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:51.670
It's getting cold... Let's go.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:53.390
Hey...

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.700
I'm going back.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.020
An illusion...

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:12.020
I want you to show me one of your illusions.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:16.880
Something so pretty, no one has ever seen it.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:19.560
I'm sorry.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:24.740
The only illusions I can show are of hell...

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:29.750
The endless hell that comes 
after the end of the world.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:32.710
It is an awful technique.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:42.470
And?

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.130
Head straight back.

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:06.830
High Priest Tenkai?

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.120
This is Namenba.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:17.410
She saved Princess Sen, granddaughter 
of His Divine Lordship Ieyasu,

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:20.260
from the burning Osaka Castle.

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:24.310
During the Osaka Summer Campaign.

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:30.630
Namenba, do you know me?

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:32.360
Yes.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.530
To borrow the words of the 
man hiding in the rafters,

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.840
you are His Holiness Nankoubou Tenkai.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:41.830
The most trusted councilor of Lord Ieyasu.

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:46.860
You were deeply involved in 
the Houkouji bell's naming

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:49.390
that led to the Osaka War.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:56.110
And Tenkai asked for help 
defeating the Joujinshuu?

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:57.960
I guess so.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:02.560
You want us, the Iga,
to help defeat the Joujinshuu?

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.860
Joujin is trying to end Tokugawa rule...

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:10.850
No, the peaceful era that has finally come...

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:13.770
to return us to the civil wars.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:18.800
This must not be allowed to happen.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:25.830
But you're aware that he and his men 
will not be easy to deal with.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.550
Indeed.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:31.390
Will you put aside our differences,

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:35.340
to fight with me, for the sake of all?

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:40.310
The Divine Lord Ieyasu did not unite Japan

00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:43.800
merely for the sake of his own ambition...

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:47.880
It was for the sake of all people.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:53.480
Jeez, you wouldn't believe the 
crap that stupid priest said.

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:57.580
Sounds like a crafty old man.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:00.470
Interesting, I suppose.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.420
Thanks, come again.

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.840
I'll take dumplings and tea.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:16.500
Sure, coming up—

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:18.790
Shichigen!

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:20.780
Make 'em piping hot.

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:50.020
We met at Takasaki, in Kouzuke.

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.540
At Tadanaga-sama's residence.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:55.420
What was Hachirou doing there?

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.590
Tadanaga-sama called him there.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:00.550
He told Hachirou to crush the Joujinshuu.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.840
And what was the reply?

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:04.620
"Hell, no."

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:08.050
And so, they attacked with rifles.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:14.760
Mere samurai can't best Hachirou 
and our techniques.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:19.000
We killed many.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.560
Where's Hachirou?

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:24.070
He said he isn't coming back.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:27.180
He'll finish this himself.

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:32.570
Right now, there's no point in thinking 
about Hachirou anymore.

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:35.830
Let's just be glad we found out where he is.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.330
Hibiki, forget him.

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:41.210
Hey, who are you?

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:45.680
I'm Ishi Saizou, one of the 
Five Treasures of Kouga.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:47.590
Got a problem?

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:48.570
What?

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:49.690
That's right.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:54.410
If that's here, he'll certainly...

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:55.650
Indeed.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:58.100
Our current job

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:02.860
is to learn more about that castle 
before Hachirou's return.

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:04.360
Agreed?

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:07.850
Indeed.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:14.660
But the Rain... What do we do about them?

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.870
I will go.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.890
Times like these...

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.560
are what I'm here for.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:05.980
Your technique really is amazing.

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:09.740
Don't worry.

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:14.040
I promise that I'll protect you.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:41.200
Who is that man?

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:43.540
I've seen him somewhere before.

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:45.760
Damn, I can't remember.

00:16:57.310 --> 00:17:03.160
How are you feeling, Kazusanosuke-sama?

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:07.090
Oda Nobunaga?

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:10.170
He died in the flames at Honnouji...

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:40.450
That was close...

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:58.720
Let's go. Hurry.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.570
They're persistent.

00:18:25.570 --> 00:18:29.700
Paddle harder, or you'll 
be caught in it, too.

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:45.830
Go.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:05.960
Is it okay, leaving it to her alone?

00:19:06.470 --> 00:19:08.040
She isn't alone.

00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:41.760
This is pretty useful.

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:51.690
It seems the weak ones have begun to stir.

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:56.770
They must be quite surprised by the 
appearance of the Murakumo.

00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:01.290
And there are more surprises in store...

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:28.770
Who are they?

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.380
The soldiers of Kishuu.

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:49.420
It seems I'd do best to hurry.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:27.010
<b><i>Preview</i></b>

00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:27.010
The twentieth year of Keichou.

00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:29.770
The Iga ninja Namenba of Otoshi

00:23:29.770 --> 00:23:33.510
saves Oichi no Kata from Osaka 
Castle, shortly before it falls.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:39.020
The war in which this occurs will later be 
called The Osaka Summer Campaign.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:38.020
<b><i>The Heavenly Robe Sees Carnage</i></b>
